{"title":"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> represents a rectangular field. There are three flagpoles: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Paul runs along the path <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe68ac3de642bf43bab0b8fc4fc96cb2bb6a293a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\to D \\to C \\to M \\to A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"192\" height=\"14\" />. Tyler runs along the path <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/2696f38503399e61f53d67422764517fa91edc78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\to P \\to Q \\to C \\to B \\to A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f7eb82948ac9d7e8659abb37508b1015d8a3cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA$\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the diagram, we can see that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a593cf705a60bf5c92a4ae50072970a12a7c06a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> in Paul's path would be a right triangle because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a rectangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/b/a6b9330726491e26a9a4c973b5e512ec42a0e782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle ABM = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"15\" />. We can then use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a> and see that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154c522b373cee41718e1d7d4563eb53a42fa060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^{2} + BM^{2} = MA^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35ef1dd6df5493380147a1c20008d56db5acddb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA^{2} = 105^{2} + 100^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40e3479d0219aad827a1fcedbda6238a29f371ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA^{2} = 11025 + 10000 = 21025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a05ef34ea30ef5b7f7857508cdd5cc7a30efa85b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04e63a6e8eb17971c96f4c13b10110e09f077d23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA = \\sqrt{21025} = \\boxed{145 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"202\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018005301\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.025 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 72/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1213/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3272/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.847      1 2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%   14.847      1 -total\n 38.30%    5.687      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36937:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018005301 and revision id 285744. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}